# Messaging & Background Jobs (Node.js)

## BullMQ (Redis)

- **Queue:** Create queue with name and connection; add jobs with data; process with worker (queue.process(handler))
- **Options:** Delay, priority, repeat (cron), jobId for idempotency; retry with backoff
- **Events:** completed, failed, stalled; use for logging and metrics
- **Concurrency:** Set concurrency per worker; use separate queues for different workloads

## Patterns

- **Fire-and-forget:** Add job and return 202; worker processes async
- **Idempotency:** Use same jobId for same logical work; dedupe in worker if needed
- **Dead letter:** After max attempts, move to DLQ or log for manual handling
- **Scheduling:** Use repeat option or separate scheduler that enqueues

## Conventions

- Validate job data in worker; keep jobs small and serializable; use correlation ID in job data for tracing; handle failures and retries

## Anti-Patterns

- Large payloads in job; no retry; no idempotency for side effects; blocking worker on long operations

